---
description: Avoid tool-brand attribution in commits, PRs, and project docs
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Tool Attribution

Do not add editor or AI-tool branding to artifacts that leave the local workstation.

- Commit messages and trailers must not include tool co-author trailers, "made with" footers, generated-by lines, or similar attribution.
- Pull request titles, bodies, review comments, and issue comments must not advertise the editor or agent used to prepare the change.
- Documentation, code comments, READMEs, and changelog entries must not credit local authoring tools.

Legitimate technical uses of lowercase words such as CSS cursor styles, database cursor APIs, pagination cursors, and required IDE configuration paths are allowed.

When asked to commit, push, or open a PR:
- Write the message/body yourself without tool trailers or footer credits.
- Use the repo hooks in `.githooks/`; do not bypass them with `--no-verify`.
- Keep PR bodies focused on product changes and verification only.
